Working for the company, I will not address that statement.  I will
point out that I use the Motif Window Manager instead.

> I know AIX and x86 Linux, but practically no experience with OSF. Does anyone
> have a pointer to some reasonably plain-English documentation on changing X
> environments under Tru64?

I set 2 lines in my .xsession:

/usr/bin//X11/mwm &
/usr/bin/X11/xterm -ls -rv -sb -sl 1000 -ms yellow -bd yellow -cr yellow
-fb 8x13 -fn 9x15bold -geometry 80x40+0+0

The first line fires up the window manager of choice (mwm in my case -
there are others) and the second puts up a window.
 
