The problem you have here is with the -x-

To quote the manpage
  x   Execute permission for files, search permission for directories.
You have to have execute permission on a directory for you to be able to
search the directory. You'll see that whilst the user adr (in group users)
has the ability to right and read files when give an absolute pathname e.g.
vi /usr/users/src/source.c (will work), they can't search (ls is a form of
search) the directory.

You need to change permission to 775. or 774 if you don't want search access
for everyone.

Robert Mulley
Unix Admin

