You will need something called "Logical Storage Manager" or "LSM."  Use
Compaq's search engine at http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com to get further
datails.  In a nutshell, spanning disks will cost you nothing, but doing
the "interesting" RAID stuff as well as using the GUI will cost you an
extra license.

Something alse you can do is to make one AdvFS domain out of one disk,
then "addvol" additional disks to the domain.  This too costs you
nothing.  Keep in mind that the AdvFS log file sits on the first disk of
the domain, so each addvol will increase the contention on that log file
and therefore on that actuator.


