I think I have found a possible problem with certain versions of 'top'
running on Tru64 5.0A.

I'd be curious if anyone else has encountered this.

I installed the latest version 3.5beta12 (ok, so it's a beta) and found
that top would nearly always report that the 'Real' memory in use was some
very large figure.

We have 2Gb RAM and even when I was the only user on the machine with just
a couple of terminals up and NOTHING else running, top would report
870-1100 Mb of memory in use.  I checked that this must be wrong by
getting top to list all processes and adding up their sizes and they
didn't come close to 870 Mb (though this depends on top reporting
individual process sizes correctly).

I tried going back and reinstalling an earlier (non-beta) version of top
(3.4) but this gave me problems when running the 'make' command.  Finally,
I went back one step and downloaded 3.5beta11 and this one seems to
behave, i.e. running top produces believable statistics.

Top can be downloaded from: ftp.groupsys.com/pub/top


Keith


