> >Sent via Deja.com http://www.deja.com/
> >Before you buy.
> 
> It sounds like the stair-stepping problem.  The text below is from the
> HP web-site.  I no longer have the URL.   On modern HP printers, you
> simply make a change on the printer itself, not on UNIX.
> 
> HP JetDirect Print Servers - Fixing Stair-stepping in UNIX (R) Print
> Jobs
> 
> QUESTION: How do I fix printing that stair-steps off of the page when
> UNIX ASCII files are sent to a printer with an HP JetDirect device?
> 
> ANSWER: Printing is done through an LPD queue, rather than a queue
> created by HP JetAdmin for UNIX. Configure a queue using the remote
> printer name "text." Send ASCII files to this queue. This requires
> creating a printcap file where the :rp= line is :rp=text:\. The remote
> printer name "text" appends a carriage return and line feed to the
> queue.
> 
> DETAILS: This is not necessary on the HP LaserJet 4000, 5000, and 8000
> printers. These printers can append a carriage return to a line feed by
> themselves:
> 
> 1. From the printer's front control panel, press the Menu button until
> Printing Menu appears.
> 
> 2. Press the Item button until APPEND CR TO LF appears.
> 
> 3. Press the Select button for an asterisk to appear on the display.
> 
> 4. Press the Go button.
> 
> For other printers, follow the steps below.
> 
> Configuring Text-Only Print Queues For BSD-Based Systems
> 
> Edit the /etc/printcap file to include the following entries:
> 
> printer_name|short_printer_name:\
> 
> :lp=:\
> 
> :rm=node_name:\
> 
> :rp=text:\
> 
> :lf=/usr/spool/lpd/error_log_filename:\
> 
> :sd=/usr/spool/lpd/printer_name:
> 
> Where printer_name identifies the printer to the user, node_name
> identifies the printer on the network, and remote_printer_name_argument
> is the print queue designation.
> 
> NOTE: To access the three ports on an HP JetDirect EX Plus3 external
> print server, choose the appropriate queue name:
> 
> Port 1 = text1
> Port 2 = text2
> Port 3 = text3


Or try using raw1 instead of text1(raw2 instead of raw2...)  If it is hp
printer with internal jd card then it is just raw or text.

Bryan



