Features such as landscape printing are provided by print filters.
To use a print filter you will need to convert your printcap entry
from lpd remote to tcp/ip printing.

Since you are using V4.0d I would try the ps_level1 and hp4mplus printer

setups. I expect both these setups will work with the HP2100 printer and

provide landscape printing. Of the two I would try the hp4mplus setup
first.
Instructions for setting up a tcp/ip queue can be found in the system
admin
book and the FAQ at www.tru64.org.

The short setup instructions:

- Edit the file /etc/services and add

        port_9100       9100/tcp

- Create a print queue for an hp4mplus printer connected to /dev/lp0.

- Edit the printcap entry
  (or set these values when using lprsetup to create the queue)

        add       :ct=tcp:\
        change :lp=@printer.com/port_9100:\
                    :pw#0:\

- The final printcap entry would look similar to the following:

        lp2|2:\
                :ct=tcp:\
                :af=/usr/adm/lp2acct:\
                :if=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Chplj4mplus.pcf:\
                :lf=/usr/adm/lp2err:\
                :lp=@printer.com/port_9100:\
                :mx#0:\
                :of=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Chplj4mplus.pcf:\
                :pl#66:\
                :pw#0:\
                :sd=/usr/spool/lpd2:\
                :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:

-------------------

