There's probably a lot you can do to tune your system - in addition to
applying the latest patch kits.  Your sys_check output shows that there
are 211 free pages and that 18K pages (over 140MB of your 704MB system
[20%]) is wired.  You need to understand if your applications really
need to wire down this much memory.  Wired memory is ineligible to page
or to be used by other processes.  If it's the lack interactive response
that you are complaining about (and it appears that you are), you can
tune the system so that it delays swapping and continues to page
instead.

Tony V.
Kernel Group



