Rolf Huebscher <choefe@gmx.ch> wrote:

>Is it possible to receive the IP address from a Windows NT DHCP server.
>What do I have to consider?

 USING DHCP Client on TRU64 Unix Directions
 
 
 STEP 1    -  EDIT (vi) /etc/hosts
 
 NOTE: THIS STEP IS NECESSARY to GET CDE on your LOGIN/CONSOLE window
            (decterm and failsafe logins will work without this step )
 
 1- vi /etc/host and put your "short" hostname in the "localhost"
string 
 
 ex:
  127.0.0.1       jones localhost
 
 
 STEP 2    - EDIT (vi)  /etc/rc.config   
 
  1 -  change your hostname to be the same hostname as in /etc/hosts
above.
       HOSTNAME="your_hostname"
 
    i.e  "your_hostname" = jones   ( your lastname, ---> not a FQDM ) 
 
  2 - Change your network settings for you NIC(s) to DYNAMIC
 
             IFCONFIG_0="DYNAMIC"
 
  3- Turn on JOIND with a "YES"
 
             JOIND="YES"
 
 
 SHUTDOWN  & REBOOT - Watch for DHCP Client IP address assignment
messages on the console as system comes up.




