X-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V5.00.2314.1300
X-Trace: fu-berlin.de 966250144 8402553 208.140.124.146 (16 [41025])
X-MSMail-Priority: Normal
Newsgroups: comp.unix.tru64

the initial values for these limits are set via /etc/sysconfigtab. See the
subsystem 'proc' for their actual values (sysconfig -q proc).
The 'per-proc-...' values are what a process gets after login. They can be
changed to lower values or upto their 'max-per-proc-...' counterparts via
the ulimit command or the setrlimit() systemcall.
The values are inherited during fork(). You can *not* change their values
from within a foreign process.

Eckhardt





