Thushara,

  The answers for finding out the space and ultimately the devices are
one and the same :-

  Use the advfs command:- /sbin/showfdmn <domain>

  This will produce the following output :-

               Id              Date Created  LogPgs  Domain Name
39940f13.00095590  Fri Aug 11 15:34:59 2000     512  testing

  Vol   512-Blks        Free  % Used  Cmode  Rblks  Wblks  Vol Name
   1L    2097152      220608     89%     on    128
128  /dev/vol/testdg/testl

  As you can see the above is an domain against an LSM volume...

  It shows you what devices are associated with the domain and their
percentage used.

Hope this is what you wanted...

Gary Hansford


