I'm not aware of a direct equivalent of Solaris' cachefs on Tru64, but the
functions of the /etc/shadow file (and many many more besides) are provided
by the enhanced security facilities.

In particular, in addition to the /etc/shadow stuff, you get:

- previous password history
- the ability to restict resource usage on a per user basis
- the inheritance of user settings from templates and system defaults that
DONT just appy at user creation time.
- the ability to choose which methods users may use to change their
passwords and a site filter to reject passwords of your choice.

I really think that these facilities in Tru64 are undersold. Check out:
http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V50A_HT
ML/ARH95BTE/TITLE.HTM
for all the details

