Hi Raymond,

For the license question, do an "lmf list" and check to see if the
licenses are there and active.  If so, you should be all set.

Regarding MS connectivity, you want ASU, aka "Advanced Server for
UNIX."  See the appropriate Web page; there's a link offering a couple
of free connects:

http://www.unix.digital.com/products/adv_server/index.html

Regarding telnetting and ftp'ing to root, T64 defaults to deny.  To
enable telnets to root, add a line to /etc/securettys as follows:

	ptys

Just adding that one "ptys" line will enable telnet sessions to root.

Then for ftp, edit the file /etc/ftpusers.  This is the file listing all
users DENIED access.  Comment out (i.e. put a # at the beginning of) the
line containing "root" and that should do it.

Hth,
WJD


