In article <01c0036e$712e00a0$29e110ac@sg02301>, "Srikanth Seshadri" <srikanth_seshadri@yahoo.com> writes:

>Hi Admins,
>I am new to Tru64. Is there a way by which I can have multiple savesets on
>a single tape. Please let me know the options for vdump/vrestore. BTW, I
>have a 35/70GB DLT tape drive.

Regardless of the command being used you can write to the no-rewind
tape special file.  For most utilities that work with tapes, the
option is usually 'f'.  See the manual page for particulars.  It
would help slightly if you could say whether you're using V4 or
something older, or V5 since that affect devices names used in
an example:

V4: vdump 0f /dev/nrmt0h /
    vdump 0f /dev/nrmt0h /usr
    vdump 0f /dev/nrmt0h /usr/users

V5: vdump 0f /dev/ntape/tape0_d0 /
    vdump 0f /dev/ntape/tape0_d0 /usr
    vdump 0f /dev/ntape/tape0_d0 /usr/users

I don't have a V5 system handy to check whether Density #0 is
really one you want to use, but the tz and mtio manual pages
should have that information.

I think vdump does have an explicit option to get the no-rewind
device, but I always use explicit device names out of habit.

