Gary Schmidt wrote:
> 
> How, programmatically _and_ portably to determine how many (physical)
> disks are attached to a Tru64 box??
> 
> In 4.x, we could loop using table(TBL_DKINFO,...), and stop on .di_name
> == "dk".
> With 5.x, it seems that  loop table(TBL_DKINFO,...) until failed, then
> decrement count by one gives the number.
> 
> I'd like to do it _one_way_ on both versions, so I don't have to be
> checking what version I'm running on (I hate parsing uname(2)).
> 
> Opinions, pointers, better ideas all welcome.
> 
>         Cheers,
>                 Gary    B-)

I hate following up myself, but this is what I've (temporarily) settled
on:

      int k, n;
      struct tbl_dkinfo dkcnt;

      /* Count disks.
       * On 4.x:       'dk' is the default disk name.
       *               Real disks will be called something different.
       * On 5.x:       We get a failure from table() after last disk
       */
      n = 0;
      dkcnt.di_name[0] = '\0';
      while ((k = table(TBL_DKINFO, n, &dkcnt, 1, sizeof(struct
tbl_dkinfo))) == 1
      && strcmp(dkcnt.di_name, "dk")) {
          ++n;
      }

	Cheers,
		Gary	B-)



