When asking O/S questions PLEASE specify the release version.  For V4x,
Eckhardt is correct in that there is a limit to the length of the
argument list.  For versions V5.0 and above,this restriction has been
removed and kernel space for arguments is allocated dynamically and you
should not hit this problem.

As a side note, some standards test suites actually depend the
limitation of kernel argument space and will fail on V5.0 and above.  A
run time configurable argument "exec_disable_arg_limit" was created to
disable dynamic arg space allocation so the tests would pass.  Run:

	sysconfig -q proc

to see your setting (V5.0 and above)

