4.0 e-g, and up to 5.0a will work on this machine.. I've done it.  You =
might try reseting your ECU, and try again.  If that doesn't work.. make =
sure your  GenVMUnix kernel can boot from the install CD.. if that =
works, then its probably some option that was set on the initial =
install.  It could be an unsupported video card.. (strange I know).  The =
newer versions of Tru64 only work with a graphics card.. if it detects =
one in your box.. it will try and use it, if it fails the boot will =
fail. Worst case just yank everything and boot from a tty.
