>
> I want to setup a time server using Tru64 v4.0f and allow an NT domain to
> use it to sync the time for the NT master time server.  Any suggestions???
>
> cheers

If you have a permanent internet connection, then configure NTP on the Tru64
system to
use a couple of external clocks, and its done, then NT can use rdate/ntp of
whatever it
wants to collect time from UNIX.


If you do not have a permanent internet connection, use NTP but with the
hardware clock as the
reference clock, its not a good as 3+ external clocks, buts its OK.

Mike





